      "message": "I believe this also affects the private range too? Also, the hypervisor will certainly map non contiguous memory range so it seems a bit difficult to interpret this way. Finally IIUC, you could end-up in the situation where you lack of memory, you think \"I\u0027ll add 1MiB more\" but then it might not change anything due to the ROUND(PTR_PER_PTE) in __hyp_pgtable_max_pages() (or will it?)\n\nI wonder if that wouldn\u0027t be easier to reason with \"the number of pages we can map in the hyp stage-1\" but then computing the worst case is a bit annoying and I do sympathize this is a \"temporary\" solution. So wouldn\u0027t that be easier to just define that as the size of the hyp stage-1 memory directly?\n\nWDYS?",
